<topic xml:id="rt-hardware-testing-install-kernel" xml:lang="en"
       role="task"
       xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.1"
       xmlns:its="http://www.w3.org/2005/11/its"
       xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"
       xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
    <info>
        <meta name="maintainer" content="daria.vladykina@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
        <title>Installing the preemptive kernel</title>
    </info>
    <para>
        Before testing latencies, you must activate the real-time capabilities 
        on your system. The preemptive kernel package provides the preemption 
        capabilities necessary for real-time operations.
    </para>
    <procedure xml:id="pro-install-preempt">
        <title>Installing and activating the kernel-preempt package</title>
        <step>
            <para>Install the preemptive kernel package:</para>
            <screen>&prompt.sudo;<command>zypper install kernel-preempt</command></screen>
        </step>
        <step>
            <para>Reboot your system.</para>
        </step>
        <step>
            <para>Select the preemptive kernel from the boot menu to activate 
                the real-time capabilities.</para>
        </step>
    </procedure>
</topic>